    {
        "content": "<p>Apparently the PBW theorem has just been formalized by AI via \"Humphreys' recursion\", see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean-eval-submissions/issues/947\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean-eval-submissions/issues/947</a></p>",
        "id": 615480979,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1786295321
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The formalized statement is PBW for a Lie algebra over a field equipped with basis <code>Fin n</code>, but the proof in Bourbaki's \"Lie Groups and Lie algebras\" Chapter 1 section 2.7 (which Humphreys faithfully copied) applies to any Lie algebra that is free over a commutative ring. That said, the formalized proof seems to be reasonably close to the text.</p>",
        "id": 615490251,
        "sender_full_name": "Scott Carnahan",
        "timestamp": 1786301673
    }
]